+### Overall score and diagnostic outcome — PO decision 2026-10-05
+
+For the user-facing overall score, a partially correct response is counted as incorrect: it contributes no positive credit to the overall score. The response remains diagnostically `partial`, and the summary identifies it as `partly correct`. Do not relabel it as fully correct or erase its omitted-element feedback. Apply the same distinction wherever a family or mode presents an overall score; keep the existing denominator and unanswered policy unless a separate approved contract changes them.
+
+This separates overall-score credit from diagnostic outcome. Saved responses and historical attempt/result evidence must not be silently rewritten or rejected merely because the current overall-score policy changed; existing verified-completion, exact-content and no-history-write contracts remain in force. Determine the minimum coherent implementation against current scoring and persisted evidence before changing runtime behavior.
+
+Authority: direct human instruction in Codex thread `01a10c6a-9012-70b3-bb15-8ca7ea944c7d`, user turn `01a10c6c-9f9f-7742-bc63-58ca9d23edf1`, verified by read-thread on 2026-10-05. This is a final product decision, not a proposal or a new release gate.
 
